w that I think that's  the realization that every student has  when they when they when they leave home  so I just started cooking and having  people over entertaining and the nice  thing about cooking is that I love three  elements of cooking shopping for  ingredients yeah cooking and then  serving because you get all these  incredible feedbacks I mean it's you  serve a good meal well and University  you had your master's degree in  philosophy your parents come from this  academic background how did you tell  them that you knew that you needed to go  into the world of could that was a bit  painful so I had my dissertation  laughter I finished studying at  University I sent it I sent it through  the post as that you did in the 90s so  my parents I was living in Europe at the  time and inside there was a little note  when hey there you go there's my  dissertation I finished my degrees but  actually not taking time off and I'm  going to learn how to cook didn't go  down very well so my you know my dad is  you know he's the gentlest nicest person  he said to me I don't know if that's  advisable his mind since he has changed  his mind yet I mean you know he's had  quite a few years to get used to the  idea and he'd seen what I've created and  how much joy I'm getting out of it but  in the beginning you described yourself  as an oddball in the kitchen mm-hmm and  you almost quit yeah kitchens are just  hard yes you know it's like it's it's  like being it's very regimented there's  a lot of shouting and screaming going on  you need to get all the food out on time  so if you are you know slightly don't  fit in it's difficult so yeah almost  left but then I discovered that I could  choose my own place so I could look I  found places that I really enjoyed  working at and that's what I always tell  young young Chefs these days don't work  where you don't want like to work  working good restaurants where you're  being respected in you and you enjoy  going to work in the morning otherwise  kind of what's the point and you have to  respect yourself I love that I love  everything about you Tom but as we  finish up our meal and our drink I would  love for you to sign the dish and think  about if there's any one person that you  would love to share this meal with okay  so I there's a argentinian chef called  francis Norman he looks yeah he's from  Patagonia down south and he does  incredible things on a barbecue and  grill I've only seen him once let met  him once for like three minutes that's  the person I would love to have Wow I  love it well so you know Tom I'm telling  you we appreciate you coming with us  you're so awesome and for more on the  chef and his fabulous dish ours as well  head to our website at CBS this morning  dot-com

